<BaseLayout title="Bike Color Identifier — Identify Motorcycle Color from Photo" description="Find the visible color of a motorcycle from a photo or camera. Sample tanks, fairings and panels to get HEX, RGB and HSL values."><div class="container"><div class="page-hero"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Bike Color Identifier</div><span class="eyebrow">For riders and motorcycle enthusiasts</span><h1>Bike Color Identifier from Photo</h1><p>Use a camera or upload a motorcycle photo to sample the visible color of a tank, fairing, fender or painted panel.</p></div><ColorIdentifier/><div class="content-layout"><article class="prose"><h2>How to identify a motorcycle color</h2><ol><li>Choose a clear photo of the painted motorcycle part.</li><li>Open the scanner and upload the photo or start the camera.</li><li>Select a representative point on the fuel tank, fairing or body panel.</li><li>Read the HEX, RGB and HSL values and save useful samples.</li></ol><h2>Get a more consistent sample</h2><p>Motorcycle surfaces are often curved and glossy. Reflections from the sky, nearby objects and bright sunlight can shift the sampled value. Take a photo in soft, even light and sample a part of the panel with minimal glare.</p><h2>Can I use this value to repaint my bike?</h2><p>Use the result as a visual digital reference only. It is not a guaranteed motorcycle factory paint code or a paint-mixing formula. For an accurate repair, confirm the OEM paint code for the exact manufacturer, model and model year, then consult a paint supplier.</p><h2>Related color tools</h2><p>Explore the <a href="/car-color-identifier/">car color identifier</a>, <a href="/color-identifier/">general color identifier</a> and <a href="/hex-to-rgb/">HEX to RGB converter</a>.</p></article><aside class="sidebar-card"><h3>Explore</h3><a href="/car-color-identifier/">Car color identifier</a><a href="/car-paint-color-codes/">Vehicle paint code guide</a><a href="/color-name-finder/">Color name finder</a><a href="/blog/">Color guides</a></aside></div></div></BaseLayout>
